{
  "title": "Femoral Shaft Stress Fractures",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3111/femoral-shaft-stress-fractures",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 1 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Femoral shaft stress fractures are overuse injuries in which abnormal stresses are placed on trabecular bone of the femoral shaft resulting in microfractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can often be made on radiographs alone but MRI studies should be obtained in patients with normal radiographs with a high degree of suspicion for stress fracture.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with protected weightbearing in young patients with good bone quality. Prophylactic intramedullary nailing is recommended in patients > 60 or those with osteopenia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in young athletic individuals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "metabolic bone disorder",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "long-term bisphosphonate use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be associated with osteopenia or osteoporosis in endurance athletes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs through crack propagation in bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "repetitive loads that exceed the threshold of intrinsic bone healing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "repetitive stress on normal bone is a **fatigue fracture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "repetitive stress on abnormal bone is an **insufficiency fracture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often a history of **overuse**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**insidious onset** of pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain during activity is localized to the involved bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain improves with rest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "focal tenderness and swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "three point **fulcrum tes**t elicits pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "examiner's arm is used as a fulcrum under the patient's thigh as gentle pressure is applied to the dorsum of the knee with the opposite hand",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "test is positive if pain and apprehension is experienced at the point of the fulcrum",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**linear cortical radiolucency**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**periosteal reaction**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fracture%20ap%20radiograph.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows a right femoral shaft stress fracture"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**endosteal and cortical thickening**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fracture.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows femoral shaft stress fractures"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fractures%20ct.jpg",
              "caption": "Shows bilateral femoral shaft stress fractures"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cortical lucency",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "benign-appearing periosteal reaction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**MRI**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most sensitive and **replacing bone scan** for diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "T2-weighted images",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fractures%20mri.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows bilateral femoral shaft stress fractures"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "findings",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "periosteal high signal is the earliest finding",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "broad area of increased signal",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "T1-weighted images",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fracture%20mri%20t1.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows bilateral femoral shaft stress fractures"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reveal linear zone of low signal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Technetium Tc 99m bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fracture%20whole%20body%20bone%20scan.jpg",
              "caption": "Shows bilateral femoral shaft stress fractures"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "focal uptake in cortical and/or trabecular bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, activity modification, protected weight bearing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most femoral shaft stress fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "restrict weight bearing until the fracture heals",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "incorporate cross-training into running programs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "locked intramedullary reconstruction nail",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3111/images/femoral%20shaft%20stress%20fracture%20imn.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows a right femoral shaft stress fracture treated with intramedullary nailing"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "prophylactic fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "patients with low bone mass",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "patients >60 years old",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fracture completion or displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reamed insertion is preferred",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Progression to complete fractures occurs if unrecognized",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
